WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:17.309
I came back to my home of Rwanda

00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:21.428
two years after the 1994 genocide
against the Tutsi.

00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:24.666
The country was devastated.

00:00:25.168 --> 00:00:28.596
The children I was caring for
in the hospitals

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.640
were dying from treatable conditions,

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:37.745
because we didn't have equipment
or medicine to save them.

00:00:39.586 --> 00:00:44.125
I was tempted to pack my bag and run away.

00:00:45.075 --> 00:00:46.942
But I debated with myself.

00:00:47.568 --> 00:00:53.609
And because I'm really dedicated
to social justice and equity,

00:00:53.633 --> 00:00:57.918
and there were only
five pediatricians in total

00:00:57.942 --> 00:01:00.902
for millions of children in Rwanda,

00:01:02.197 --> 00:01:03.800
I decided to stay.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:11.409
But among the people
who have motivated my decision to stay,

00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:14.715
there were some fantastic women of Rwanda,

00:01:15.427 --> 00:01:22.381
some women who had faced
the genocide and survived it.

00:01:23.355 --> 00:01:29.593
They had to overcome
unbelievable pain and suffering.

00:01:29.617 --> 00:01:36.524
Some of them were raising children
conceived through rape.

00:01:37.301 --> 00:01:41.475
Others were dying slowly with HIV

00:01:41.499 --> 00:01:47.142
and forgave the perpetrators,
who voluntarily infected them

00:01:47.166 --> 00:01:49.995
using HIV and rape as a weapon.

00:01:51.937 --> 00:01:54.349
So, they inspired me.

00:01:54.373 --> 00:01:55.929
If they can do that,

00:01:55.953 --> 00:01:58.825
I can stay and try to do my best.

00:02:00.336 --> 00:02:04.415
Those ladies were really activists

00:02:04.439 --> 00:02:07.177
of peace and reconciliation.

00:02:07.201 --> 00:02:10.588
They show us a way
to rebuild a country

00:02:10.612 --> 00:02:14.605
for our children and grandchildren
to have, one day,

00:02:14.629 --> 00:02:17.913
a place they can call home, with pride.

00:02:19.691 --> 00:02:23.201
And you can ask yourself

00:02:24.318 --> 00:02:28.508
where this shift of mindset
has brought our country.

00:02:30.288 --> 00:02:32.255
Today in Rwanda,

00:02:32.279 --> 00:02:38.906
we have the highest percentage
of women in parliament.

00:02:39.823 --> 00:02:42.061
(Applause)

00:02:42.085 --> 00:02:44.934
Wait till I tell you the percentage --

00:02:44.958 --> 00:02:47.061
sixty-one percent.

00:02:47.085 --> 00:02:50.149
(Applause)

00:02:50.173 --> 00:02:55.815
Today, we have the best campaign
for the vaccination of children

00:02:55.839 --> 00:03:02.521
with, among our success, 93 percent
of our girls vaccinated against HPV --

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.830
(Applause)

00:03:04.854 --> 00:03:08.115
to protect them against cervical cancer.

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:10.789
In this country, it's 54.

00:03:11.305 --> 00:03:12.781
(Laughter)

00:03:13.425 --> 00:03:17.810
We have reduced
child mortality by 75 percent,

00:03:18.429 --> 00:03:21.230
maternal mortality by 80 percent.

00:03:21.659 --> 00:03:23.516
In early 2000s,

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.505
there were nine women
who were dying every day

00:03:27.529 --> 00:03:30.646
around delivery and pregnancy.

00:03:31.006 --> 00:03:32.767
Today, it's around two.

00:03:33.517 --> 00:03:35.358
It's an unfinished agenda.

00:03:35.382 --> 00:03:37.596
We still have a long way to go.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.437
Two is still too much.

00:03:42.915 --> 00:03:49.193
But, do I believe that those results

00:03:49.217 --> 00:03:54.352
are because we had a big number of women

00:03:54.376 --> 00:03:55.880
in power positions?

00:03:56.749 --> 00:03:57.923
I do.

00:03:57.947 --> 00:03:59.598
(Laughter)

00:03:59.622 --> 00:04:00.878
There is -- yes --

00:04:00.902 --> 00:04:02.491
(Applause)

00:04:02.515 --> 00:04:05.115
there is a study in the developing world

00:04:05.139 --> 00:04:10.855
that shows that if you improve
the status of women,

00:04:10.879 --> 00:04:14.728
you improve the status
of the community where they live.

00:04:15.601 --> 00:04:20.805
Up to 47 percent of decrease
in child mortality.

00:04:21.574 --> 00:04:24.375
And even in this country where we are now,

00:04:24.399 --> 00:04:25.549
it's true.

00:04:26.018 --> 00:04:30.410
There is a study by a lady
called Patricia Homan,

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:34.974
who projected that if women and men

00:04:34.998 --> 00:04:39.156
were at parity in state legislatures,

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:44.425
there would be a drop of 14.5 percent
in child mortality --

00:04:44.449 --> 00:04:45.767
in America!

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:51.410
So we know that women,

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:55.270
when they use their skills
in leadership positions,

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:59.111
they enhance the entire population
they are in charge of.

00:05:00.093 --> 00:05:03.474
And imagine what would happen

00:05:03.498 --> 00:05:08.228
if women were at parity with men
all over the world.

00:05:08.252 --> 00:05:11.195
What a huge benefit we could expect.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:12.940
Hmm?

00:05:13.282 --> 00:05:14.433
Oh, yeah.

00:05:14.457 --> 00:05:16.020
(Applause)

00:05:16.044 --> 00:05:18.337
Because in general,

00:05:18.361 --> 00:05:20.742
we have a different style of leadership:

00:05:21.457 --> 00:05:23.164
more inclusive,

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:24.934
more empathetic,

00:05:24.958 --> 00:05:27.664
more caring for little children.

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:30.450
And this makes the difference.

00:05:32.294 --> 00:05:37.841
Unfortunately, this ideal
doesn't exist in the world,

00:05:37.865 --> 00:05:43.366
and the difference between men and women
in leadership positions

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:45.382
is too big.

00:05:45.768 --> 00:05:50.944
Gender inequity is the norm
in the majority of professions,

00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:52.975
even in global health.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:06:00.612
I have learned that if we focus
on women's education,

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:05.435
we improve their life positively

00:06:05.459 --> 00:06:08.387
as well as the well-being
of their community.

00:06:08.793 --> 00:06:14.030
This is why now I dedicate
my life to education.

00:06:14.658 --> 00:06:20.229
And this is totally aligned
with my sense of equity

00:06:20.253 --> 00:06:23.490
and my pursuit of social justice,

00:06:23.514 --> 00:06:30.045
because if you want to increase
access to health services,

00:06:30.069 --> 00:06:33.806
you need first to increase
access to health education.

00:06:34.538 --> 00:06:39.403
So with friends and partners,
we are building a beautiful university

00:06:39.427 --> 00:06:41.293
in the rural north of Rwanda.

00:06:41.895 --> 00:06:45.152
We educate our students

00:06:45.176 --> 00:06:51.232
to provide quality,
equitable, holistic care

00:06:51.256 --> 00:06:54.303
to everyone, leaving no one out,

00:06:55.034 --> 00:06:59.298
focusing on the vulnerable,
especially women and children,

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:03.827
who are historically
the last to be served.

00:07:05.284 --> 00:07:07.592
We transform them into leaders

00:07:07.616 --> 00:07:11.808
and give them managerial skills
and advocacy skills

00:07:11.832 --> 00:07:15.666
for them to be smooth changemakers

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:17.808
in the society where they will be,

00:07:17.832 --> 00:07:20.427
so that they can build health systems

00:07:20.451 --> 00:07:24.376
that allow them to care
about the vulnerable where they are.

00:07:25.235 --> 00:07:27.427
And it's really transformative.

00:07:28.234 --> 00:07:31.054
Because currently,

00:07:32.362 --> 00:07:34.434
medical education, for example,

00:07:34.458 --> 00:07:38.776
is given in institutions based in cities,

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:45.292
focused on quality health services
and skills, clinical skills,

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:49.316
to be given in institutions.

00:07:50.498 --> 00:07:55.398
We also focus on quality clinical skills

00:07:55.422 --> 00:08:00.906
but with biosocial approach
to the condition of patient,

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:06.113
for care to be given in communities
where the people live,

00:08:06.137 --> 00:08:09.351
with hospitalization only when necessary.

00:08:11.066 --> 00:08:12.268
And also,

00:08:12.292 --> 00:08:18.410
after four to seven years
of clinical education in cities,

00:08:18.434 --> 00:08:22.252
young graduates don't want
to go back to rural area.

00:08:23.729 --> 00:08:30.356
So this is why we have built
the University of Global Health Equity,

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:34.196
an initiative of Partners
in Health, called UGHE,

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:36.338
in the rural north of Rwanda.

00:08:37.172 --> 00:08:42.434
(Applause)

00:08:42.982 --> 00:08:44.501
Our students

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:48.411
are meant to go and change the world.

00:08:49.498 --> 00:08:53.688
They will come from all over --
it's a global university --

00:08:53.712 --> 00:08:56.903
and will get the medical
education for free

00:08:56.927 --> 00:08:58.904
at one condition:

00:08:58.928 --> 00:09:02.975
they have to serve the vulnerable
across the world

00:09:02.999 --> 00:09:05.046
during six to nine years.

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:08.585
They will keep the salary
for themselves and their families

00:09:08.609 --> 00:09:12.688
but turn the education we give
in quality clinical services,

00:09:12.712 --> 00:09:14.579
especially for the vulnerable.

00:09:15.839 --> 00:09:18.998
And doing so,

00:09:19.022 --> 00:09:24.323
they sign an agreement at the start
that they will do that,

00:09:24.347 --> 00:09:26.395
a binding agreement.

00:09:26.419 --> 00:09:27.966
We don't want money.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:30.457
We have to go and mobilize the money.

00:09:30.919 --> 00:09:36.463
But they will turn this
in quality service delivery for all.

00:09:39.426 --> 00:09:41.053
For this, of course,

00:09:41.077 --> 00:09:44.553
we need a strong gender equity agenda.

00:09:45.141 --> 00:09:48.632
And in all our classes, master's course,

00:09:48.656 --> 00:09:51.362
minimum of 50 percent of women.

00:09:52.474 --> 00:09:56.237
(Applause)

00:09:56.261 --> 00:09:58.285
And I'm proud to say

00:09:58.309 --> 00:10:02.483
that for the medical school
that started five months ago,

00:10:02.507 --> 00:10:06.025
we have enrolled 70 percent girls.

00:10:06.049 --> 00:10:09.334
(Applause)

00:10:09.358 --> 00:10:13.493
This is a statement against
the current inequity

00:10:13.517 --> 00:10:18.078
for women to access
medical education in our continent.

00:10:20.245 --> 00:10:25.047
I believe in women's education.

00:10:25.071 --> 00:10:30.140
This is why I applaud African ladies
who go all over the world

00:10:30.164 --> 00:10:33.688
to increase their education,
their skills and their knowledge.

00:10:33.712 --> 00:10:37.071
But I hope they will bring
that back to Africa

00:10:37.095 --> 00:10:39.331
to build the continent

00:10:39.355 --> 00:10:42.172
and make the continent a strong continent,

00:10:42.196 --> 00:10:43.848
because I'm sure

00:10:45.101 --> 00:10:48.553
a stronger Africa
will make the world stronger.

00:10:50.602 --> 00:10:54.969
(Applause)

00:10:57.088 --> 00:10:59.398
Twenty-three years ago,

00:10:59.422 --> 00:11:02.493
I went back to Rwanda,

00:11:02.517 --> 00:11:04.318
to a broken Rwanda,

00:11:04.342 --> 00:11:06.580
that now is still a poor country

00:11:06.604 --> 00:11:10.249
but shining with a bright future.

00:11:10.667 --> 00:11:13.463
And I am full of joy to have come back,

00:11:13.487 --> 00:11:15.774
even if some days were very difficult,

00:11:15.798 --> 00:11:19.944
and even if some days I was depressed,
because I didn't find a solution

00:11:19.968 --> 00:11:21.338
and people were dying,

00:11:21.362 --> 00:11:23.874
or things were not moving enough.

00:11:25.519 --> 00:11:30.003
But I'm so proud to have contributed
to improve my community.

00:11:30.995 --> 00:11:33.558
And this makes me full of joy.

00:11:34.395 --> 00:11:38.172
So, African women from the diaspora,

00:11:39.418 --> 00:11:41.069
if you hear me,

00:11:41.093 --> 00:11:43.934
never forget your homeland.

00:11:44.955 --> 00:11:47.742
And when you are ready, come back home.

00:11:49.645 --> 00:11:50.795
I did so.

00:11:51.971 --> 00:11:54.486
It has fulfilled my life.

00:11:54.889 --> 00:11:57.471
So, come back home.

00:11:57.802 --> 00:11:58.976
Thank you.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.730
(Applause)

